{"id": "e15a1125-a436-4d10-833a-44e8a78840e9", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T15:41:33.161310", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "fdbcce2e-3e3b-45a5-8864-03f464cef4b3", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "From here I'll use these pre-computed predictions (labeled as such) to write up the final design in Spanish with compact tables. I'll hand it off with stage=result.

Structure:
(a) Rationale per arm
(b) Table of confounder controls
(c) Operational analysis plan: statistical model, what to falsify/confirm
(d) Feasibility (budget tier) + what can be realized here
(e) Labeling rules

Keep it compact. All numbers: FLOPs/GPU-hour tables labeled as "expected predictions (6ND formula, arithmetic calculation, not an executed experiment)", benchmark numbers as "reported values (source)".

Reported values from Llama-2 paper (Touvron et al. 2023, arXiv:2307.09288, table numbers as I remember them): Llama-2-13B MMLU 55.9, 70B 68.9; GSM8K 13B 28.7? Actually Llama-2 13B GSM8K 30.2? Careful — label as approximate reported values. Known from the paper (Table 3): Llama-2 7B: MMLU 46.8; 13B: 55.0; 70B: 68.9. GSM8K: 7B 14.0, 13B 28.7, 70B 56.8. HumanEval: 7B 12.2? Actually 12.2? Llama-2 7B HumanEval 12.2, 13B 18.3? Hmm, Llama-2 paper: HumanEval 7B 12.2, 13B 18.8, 70B 32.3? Not confident. I'll only cite MMLU and GSM8K, which are well remembered: MMLU 46.8/55.0/68.9, GSM8K 14.0/28.7/56.8. And for Chat versions: MMLU chat is slightly lower than base (e.g., 70B-chat 67.7 vs base 68.9 — I recall there's an alignment tax on MMLU). This is a useful point: the alignment tax on knowledge benchmarks. Label as "reported values (approx., main text; to be cross-checked when executing Arm C)". Uncertainty should be honest: when executing, verify numbers against source tables.

TruthfulQA: Llama-2 70B 53.9? Not confident. Skip it, or mark as to-be-verified.

Also Chinchilla: Chinchilla 70B was trained on 1.4T tokens, and outperformed Gopher 280B trained on 300B tokens — a literature example where smaller size + more tokens wins (Hoffmann et al. 2022). This is the anchor of the headline evidence.

Zephyr-7B-DPO outperforms Llama-2-70B-chat on some benchmarks (Zephyr paper, Tunstall et al. 2023) — MT-Bench 7.3 vs Llama-2-70b-chat 6.2? I recall Zephyr 7B's MT-Bench is ~7.35, and Llama-2-70b-chat is ~6.27. Label as approximate reported value.

Design details:

Arm A: Ladder {300M, 1B, 3B, 7B} × {2, 20, 100 tok/param}, identical tokenizer (e.g., Llama BPE 32k), identical data (SlimPajama/C4 deduplicated), shared-prefix curriculum, 3 seeds at the smallest scale, 1 seed for 7B. Alignment sub-arm only at 1B/3B: base → SFT (few thousand Dolly/FLAN instructions) → DPO (few thousand preference pairs). Evaluation: perplexity + benchmark suite.

Arm B: Published checkpoints: Llama-2 {7,13,70}B base vs chat; + external references: Mistral-7B-Instruct, Zephyr-7B-DPO, as "small aligned vs large unaligned/large".

Arm C: Literature audit: scaling curve from Hoffmann 2022; crossover of Chinchilla 70B vs Gopher 280B; Llama-2 base vs chat tables; alignment tax.

Analysis plan:
- Primary model: mixed-effects lmer: score_ijkm = β0 + β1·log(N) + β2·log(D) + β3·log(N)×log(D) + β4·alignment + u_benchmark + item bootstrap. Falsification of strict monotonicity: significant negative simple effect of size at fixed low D; or pairwise test: under-trained larger model < compute-optimal smaller model, Bonferroni/Holm-corrected, one-sided, effect size > 1 point on the primary suite.
- Confirmation of monotonicity: all significant contrasts favor larger size across all (size, alignment) combinations; monotone non-decreasing pattern on Arm C curves within the same model family.
- Bayesian secondary analysis: P(monotonicity | data) via isotonic regression.
- Falsification criteria are set in advance.

Budget tiers:
- T0 (this environment): Arm C only — arithmetic is realizable here (6ND table already computed; labeled as projection).
- T1 small proxy: 300M–1B × 3 budgets ≈ 350 A100-hours (sum: 2.4+24+120+26.7+267+1335 ≈ 1776? Don't sum incorrectly: the full ladder 300M+1B is ~1776 GPU-hours; the infra+optimo subset is ~320). Present the per-cell numbers from the computed table as-is and show the range.
- T2 medium: +3B, 7B infra/optimo: +~17k GPU-hours.
- T3 full: +70B (130k–6.5M GPU-hours) — infeasible without a national-scale budget; that's precisely why the causal arm uses small sizes + 13B/70B literature is treated as observational anchor.

Data requirements: deduplicated SlimPajama 1.2T tokens or C4; for the proxy's infra budget only a portion is needed.

GQA limitation + sensitivity analysis: compare a non-GQA family (Mistral-7B is also GQA… Mistral uses GQA. Non-GQA: Llama-1/LLaMA original, OPT, Pythia (no GQA), MPT). Use the Pythia suite (trained on 300B tokens, sizes 70M–12.7B, standardized training) — actually the Pythia suite is ideal for Arm A/C: 16 published sizes trained on identical data and order, with intermediate checkpoints! A perfect anchor for "compute ladder" literature audit. Mention Pythia (Biderman et al. 2023) as sensitivity family without GQA.

TruthfulQA/hallucination metrics are fine.

The deliverable will be written in stage=result. Compact tables.
", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bd9d3f21239c6fd5", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-bd9d3f21239c6fd5", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"answer": "# DISEÑO FINAL (solo diseño — ningún experimento fue ejecutado; ninguna cifra presentada como medida propia)\n\n**Pregunta:** ¿más parámetros ⇒ siempre más rendimiento, o pueden el pre-entrenamiento insuficiente y la falta de alineación fina anular la ventaja de un modelo mayor (p. ej. 70B vs 13B)?\n**Hipótesis nula a falsar:** monotonía estricta tamaño→rendimiento para familia/datos/harness fijos.\n\n## (a) Brazos y racional\n\n| Brazo | Qué hace | Racional | Estatus |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **A (causal, proxy)** | Escalera {300M, 1B, 3B, 7B} × presupuesto de tokens {~2 (infra), ~20 (compute-óptimo, Chinchilla), ~100 (sobre-entrenado)} tok/parám.; misma familia arquitectónica y tokenizer. Sub-eje de alineación solo en 1B/3B: base → SFT (~5k instrucciones) → DPO (~5k pares de preferencia). | Único brazo con manipulación real de tamaño×tokens×alineación; identifica la interacción que prueba/falsa la monotonía. Escala ≤7B porque 70B desde cero es inviable (ver d). | Diseño para cómputo externo |\n| **B (observacional, checkpoints publicados)** | Llama-2 {7B, 13B, 70B} base vs chat (SFT+RLHF) + referencias externas pequeño-alineado: Zephyr-7B-DPO, Mistral-7B-Instruct. | Separa el efecto de alineación sin entrenamiento propio; prueba si un 7B alineado supera a 13B/70B no alineados en tareas sensibles a alineación (y si persiste la \"align tax\" en conocimiento). | Analizable fuera de este sandbox (pesos restringidos) |\n| **C (auditoría de literatura — NÚCLEO demostrable)** | Re-análisis de cifras publicadas: tablas Llama-2 (Touvron et al. 2023, arXiv:2307.09288); curvas Chinchilla (Hoffmann et al. 2022: Chinchilla-70B-1.4T tok supera a Gopher-280B-300B tok = cruce ya reportad